---
output: svg
---
@startuml
' issue #2679: GroupBorderThickness only ever converted to LineThickness on
' the "group" style (see FromSkinparamToStyle), never on "groupHeader". A
' partition read its border stroke from "groupHeader", so this skinparam
' had no visible effect on a partition's border even though it worked for
' a plain group's.
'
' Now that "partition" is its own dedicated style selector (decoupled from
' "group" per #2679's resolution), the legacy skinparam -- which only ever
' bridged to "group"/"groupHeader" -- has no bridge to "partition" at all.
' Styling a partition's border now goes exclusively through <style>. Pins
' that route works, and that the legacy skinparam correctly leaves the
' partition's border alone (only the plain group is affected by it).
skinparam sequence {
    GroupBorderColor #FF0000
    GroupBorderThickness 6
}
<style>
sequenceDiagram {
  partition {
    LineColor #FF0000
    LineThickness 6
  }
}
</style>
actor User
participant System

group Setup (group)
User -> System : init()
end

partition Setup (partition)
User -> System : init()
end
@enduml
